# The launch gate check (CAP-012, docs/authority-model.md 7.5; headless
# --test launch-gate): a requester holding procmgr's endpoint and a Launch
# badge into the user session (optional, so this check also runs where no
# badge exists and says what fails). Its table names two children and
# capability-test.app, which asks for nothing. A small handle limit lets it count its
# free handle places before and after launching.
(Executable_Manifest
  identity => "com.cubit.test.launch-gate"
  version => "1.0.0"
  requests => [
    (service "logstore" "logstore")
    (service "process-manager" "process-manager")
    (service "launch" "launch")
    # Section 6: the session's debug authority (DBG-001) and a system
    # service to observe through it.
    (service "debug-session" "debug-session")
    (service "clock" "clock")]
  optional => ["launch" "debug-session"]
  handles => (Handle_Limit.At_Most 16)
  may_launch => [(Launch "launch-gate-child.app") (Launch "launch-gate-greedy.app")
    (Launch "capability-test.app")])
